{
  "about": "The restore class of the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.4, 6.9, 6.11; WP1): items the robot must not leave open (house.left_open) nor hold open past a limit (house.held_open): exterior doors, gates, pet / child / pool gates, fire doors, fridges, freezers, ovens, dishwashers, safes and medicine cabinets -- no windows (6.9; a window's open is an ordinary setting, house.changed). Each class lists the entity types, categories, is_a names or fields that select it (exclude_fields: values that unselect it, e.g. the exterior windows) and its hold limit in seconds; a record belongs to the first class it matches in this order (a gate, exterior: true, is taken by the exterior-door rule first: the same 300 s hold). The effective limit is max(hold_s, reference_factor x the reference's longest robot-attributable interval for that item). A gate class whose zero_when_protected is true has a limit of 0 s while a protected agent (people: a child under child_age or a person flagged wandering; pets: escape_risk_flags) is in the gate's connected zone and the robot is not within near_m of the gate. open_paths: the fields house.left_open judges for a restore-class item (house.changed leaves them to it).",
